## Constraints & Assumptions

- **C-01**: Language for the agent script — the repo has Python (`app/`) and TypeScript (`infra/`). Assumption: the agent will be implemented in **Python** (consistent with existing app + Hypothesis for PBT), to be confirmed in NFR Requirements/tech-stack stage.
- **C-02**: Authentication for the review engine uses `KIRO_API_KEY` retrieved at runtime from **AWS Secrets Manager** via the existing **OIDC** federation (short-lived STS credentials). No static key is stored in GitHub. A least-privilege IAM permission (`secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` on the specific secret ARN) is added — either a new dedicated review role or a scoped policy (decided in Infrastructure Design). The `GitHubActionsDeployRole`/deploy OIDC flow remains unchanged.
- **C-03**: The existing branch protection on `dev`/`main` must be configured to require the new status check for FR-06 to actually block merges (a repo settings step — documented, not code).
- **C-04**: The Kiro CLI binary must be available on the CodeBuild runner (installed as a pinned version in the workflow) and support `chat --no-interactive`. The Kiro key secret must be created in AWS Secrets Manager (one-time bootstrap, documented).

---

## Key Requirements Summary

The feature adds an autonomous, **Kiro CLI (headless)**-powered code reviewer that runs as a new GitHub Actions workflow (on the existing CodeBuild runner) for every PR to `dev`. It reviews quality, correctness, and security; posts summary + inline comments; **blocks merge via a required status check on high-severity findings**; and **auto-approves** clean PRs. Authentication keeps the OIDC-only posture: the `KIRO_API_KEY` is stored in **AWS Secrets Manager** and fetched at runtime via the OIDC role (no static key in GitHub). Security Baseline and (full) Property-Based Testing extensions are enforced as blocking constraints; Resiliency is opt-out.

